{"id":4593047,"accountId":29,"type":"text","title":"Ningbo: Dates, who's playing, prize money and everything to know","description":"The BNB Ningbo Open serves as the second-to-last WTA 500 event of the season, and is currently headlined by Elena Rybakina, Elina Svitolina, Iga Swiatek and more. Here is everything you need to know.","date":"2026-10-16T13:30:00Z","location":"","coordinates":[0.0,0.0],"commentsOn":false,"copyright":null,"publishFrom":1792116664209,"publishTo":0,"tags":[{"id":11645,"label":"Tournament News"},{"id":4886,"label":"News"}],"platform":"PULSE_CMS","language":"en","additionalInfo":{},"canonicalUrl":"","references":[{"label":null,"id":4447270,"type":"BIO","sid":"4447270"},{"label":null,"id":2092,"type":"TENNIS_TOURNAMENTGROUP","sid":"2092"}],"related":[{"label":"Kartal’s comeback gathers pace with landmark run to Wuhan final","id":4593140,"type":"TEXT","sid":"4593140"},{"label":"'150 percent of your focus': Andreeva on what it will take to compete at the WTA Finals","id":4591278,"type":"TEXT","sid":"4591278"},{"label":"Zheng Qinwen to miss Japan Open with continued shoulder injury","id":4592910,"type":"TEXT","sid":"4592910"}],"metadata":{},"titleTranslations":null,"lastModified":1792156641929,"titleUrlSegment":"ningbo-open-2026-everything-to-know-dates-prize-money-who-is-playing","visibilityOrder":[],"allowedUserGroups":[],"allowedTerritories":[],"body":"<p>Following the final WTA 1000 event of the season in Wuhan, the WTA Tour Driven by Mercedes-Benz continues with the BNB Ningbo Open. </p>\n<p>Ningbo plays host to the penultimate WTA 500 event of the season, and 2026 marks its third edition of a tournament at the level. Defending champion and World No. 1 Elena Rybakina headlines the field as she builds up to the 2026 WTA Finals at Indian Wells. </p>\n<p>Here's everything to know about this year's Ningbo Open:</p>\n<h4>What are the dates for each round?</h4>\n<p>Main draw play from Ningbo begins Monday, October 19, and ends with the championships on Sunday, October 25. The doubles final will be held at 2:30 p.m. local time, with the singles final to follow, not before 5 p.m.</p><div class=\"articleWidget center\">\n</div><p><strong>Time conversions: </strong>5 p.m. China Standard Time = 5 a.m. Eastern Time, 9 a.m. Greenwich Mean Time</p>\n<h5>Singles</h5>\n<p><strong>First round: </strong>October 19-20<br /><strong>Second round:</strong> October 21-22<br /><strong>Quarterfinals:</strong> October 23<br /><strong>Semifinals:</strong> October 24<br /><strong>Final:</strong> October 25</p>\n<h5>Doubles</h5>\n<p><strong>First round:</strong> October 29-21<br /><strong>Quarterfinals:</strong> October 22-22<br /><strong>Semifinals:</strong> October 24<br /><strong>Final:</strong> October 25</p>\n<h4>How big is the draw, and who are the top players in the field?</h4>\n<p>Ningbo will feature a 28-player singles draw and 16-team doubles draw. The top four singles players at the time of seeding will receive byes into the second round. </p>\n<p><strong>Projected seeded players</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Elena Rybakina</li>\n<li>Elina Svitolina</li>\n<li>Iga Swiatek</li>\n<li>Marta Kostyuk</li>\n<li>Iva Jovic</li>\n<li>Belinda Bencic</li>\n<li>Diana Shnaider</li>\n<li>Elise Mertens</li>\n</ol><div class=\"articleWidget center\">\n        <aside class=\"instagram-post embeddable-widget embeddable-widget--floating embeddable-widget--centered-mobile \"><blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DP_UfsTksuz/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\" style=\" background:#FFF; border:0; border-radius:3px; box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15); margin: 1px; max-width:540px; min-width:326px; padding:0; width:99.375%; width:-webkit-calc(100% - 2px); width:calc(100% - 2px);\"><div style=\"padding:16px;\"> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DP_UfsTksuz/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=l